<title>UK: TransCo UK gas forecasts for April 3.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas forecasts for April 3.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Tuesday published the following data and forecasts for gas use in the period April 1 to 3.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = millon cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 01 (actual) 209 mcm, 49 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 02 (forecast) 214 mcm, 50 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 03 (forecast) 230 mcm, 54 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Apr 01 (actual) 10.4 Celsius, seasonal normal 8.0 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 02 (forecast) 10.8 Celsius, seasonal normal 8.1 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 03 (forecast) 8.1 Celsius, seasonal normal 8.2 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption on Wednesday, with none expected on Thursday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5387</p>
</text>
